The running thread counts as alone while another share waits on the run queue.
The timer would let the ticks pass that end the turn, and the other share would wait until the account ran low;
every tick the timer lets pass hands the processor back to the running thread.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-grain32 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: the timer lets a tick pass that ends the turn

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -474,7 +474,7 @@ static void tick_advance(uint32_t ticks)
  */
 uint32_t sched_wake_ticks(void)
 {
-    if (turn != NULL && (thread_share(current) != turn || turn->threads != 0 || run_queue != NULL)) {
+    if (turn != NULL && (thread_share(current) != turn || turn->threads != 0)) {
         return 1;
     }
     uint32_t wake = nearest_deadline - sched_ticks;
